    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "It has been numerically studied that for the Poisson model problem, the trained solution U(x;θP) with the PINN loss JP,M(θ) gives better training results than the trained solution U(x;θR) with the deep Ritz loss JR,M(θ); see [40]. In our work, we will reinvestigate the performance of the two approaches for various hyper parameter settings and report some of our new ﬁndings."
