    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "We note that the above optimization problems for θ are non-linear and non-convex while those for λ are linear. We thus use the Adam optimization method [20] in the gradient update for θ with a small learning rate ǫ and a simple gradient update for λ with a learning rate α, i.e.,"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 57,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 71.64, 97.829, 540.156, 152.552 ],
    "font" : "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "λ = λ + α∇λLP,M or λ = λ + α∇λLR,M. The learning rate α is often set to a larger value than the learning rate ǫ, as proposed in two-scale update schemes for min-max optimization problems; see [14, 25, 7]. In our numerical experiments, we set ǫ = 0.001 for the Adam optimizer and α = 1 for the gradient ascent update."
